<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ecbatana</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ecbatana, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamadan">Hamadan</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/median-empire">Median Empire</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> conquered Media, it became one of the royal residences and administrative centres of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>, used especially as a summer capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ecbatana.jpg" alt="Ecbatana" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Behzad39 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hegmataneh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Persepolis was the ceremonial capital where the empire's subject nations presented tribute, Susa the principal administrative centre and <b>Ecbatana</b> the summer residence.</blockquote><a href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Herodotus credits Deioces (traditionally r. c. 700–675 BCE) with uniting the Median clans and founding <b>Ecbatana</b> (modern Hamadan) as the capital.</blockquote><a href="/empire/median-empire">Median Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The royal court moved between residences such as Ctesiphon, <b>Ecbatana</b> and Hecatompylos, and effective government depended on negotiation and alliance-building with regional elites.</blockquote><a href="/empire/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>His court moved between Persepolis, Susa, <b>Ecbatana</b> and Babylon, and the reliefs of the Apadana at Persepolis show delegations of the subject peoples bringing him gifts.</blockquote><a href="/societies/achaemenid-persia">Social Hierarchy of the Achaemenid Empire</a></li><li><blockquote>In 550 BCE Cyrus II, king of Anshan, defeated the Median king Astyages and took <b>Ecbatana</b>, then went on to found the Achaemenid Empire.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-anshan">Kingdom of Anshan</a></li></ul></section>
